<title>FRANCE: Canal Plus sees break-even in 1997.</title>
<headline>Canal Plus sees break-even in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canal Plus finance director Laurent Perpere told analysts on Monday that the group expected to break even in 1997, excluding exceptional items, a spokesman for Canal Plus said.</p>
<p>Prior to Canal Plus's announcement on Friday of plans to merge with Nethold, analysts were expecting a profit for 1997 of between 700 million and 800 million francs.</p>
<p>Perpere said there would be a mild dilution in per-share earnings until the year 2000 as a result of the merger.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
